-- title:
--   Two representatives of a class of J₀(N) differ by a principal divisor
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and let $\bar F_N$ denote `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the compositum over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field $\mathbb Q(\text{divisorExpansions } N)$; divisors are finitely supported $\mathbb Z$-valued functions on the set of places of $\bar F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (valuation subrings, proper, containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and with principal ideals), and $J_0(N)$ is the quotient of the degree-zero divisors by the principal ones. Let $K$ be a finite-dimensional intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $c$ be an element of $J_0(N)$ fixed by the action, through `arithmeticGalois`, of the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ fixing $K$ pointwise. Let $D, D'$ be divisors of $\bar F_N$ each satisfying `JZero.IsRepOf N K n c`, i.e. each is effective, each is invariant under the above Galois action restricted to the fixing subgroup of $K$, and each is of the form $E + n\,\overline{\infty}$ with $E$ of degree $0$ whose class in $J_0(N)$ is $c$, where $\overline{\infty}$ is the place `cuspInftyBar N`. The conclusion is that $D' - D$ is principal: there is an $f \ne 0$ in $\bar F_N$ with $(D'-D)(v) = \mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$.
--
--   This is the elementary linear-equivalence fact underlying all comparisons of two representatives of one point of $J_0(N)$: the moving function $f$ it produces lies in the Riemann–Roch space of the effective representative. It is used in the construction of representatives with controlled multiplicity at the cusp $\overline{\infty}$, via [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_isRepOf_forall_apply_cuspInftyBar_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_isRepOf_forall_apply_cuspInftyBar_le).
